Third-party software
--------------------

This package depends on, and does not bundle, the following libraries. Each is
installed separately under its own licence.

1. pyerfa (BSD-3-Clause)
   Python wrapper for the ERFA library. ERFA is derived from the IAU SOFA
   library but is not SOFA. Nothing in this package is endorsed by the
   International Astronomical Union or by the SOFA Board.

2. jplephem (MIT License)
   Reader for JPL SPK ephemeris kernel files.

3. numpy (BSD-3-Clause, with some bundled components under other permissive
   licences; see the numpy distribution for details)

4. tzdata (Apache-2.0)
   IANA time zone database packaged for Python, used where the operating
   system provides none.

Ephemeris kernels
-----------------

JPL planetary ephemerides are downloaded from NASA NAIF at run time and are not
redistributed in this package. Their use does not imply endorsement of this
package by NASA, JPL or NAIF.

US Naval Observatory data used only in the separate accuracy study are public-domain government data; the study and bulk kernels are not bundled in the wheel.
